  "notes": "Prospective n-of-1 study. Every reading comes from a real YouCam Skin Analysis call on a real capture session; nothing is generated or illustrative. Face images are never committed, only the scores the API returned, so the dataset is auditable without publishing anyone photograph. Calibration sessions are sampled from separate windows of one continuous recording, which captures pose and distance drift between sessions but not the error of moving the camera itself, so the floor it yields is a lower bound on full repositioning error.",
  "concerns": [
    "texture",
    "redness",
    "moisture",
    "acne",
    "pore",
    "radiance"
  ],
  "products": [
    {
      "id": "dove-men-care-extra-fresh-wash",
      "name": "Dove Men+Care Extra Fresh Body & Face Wash",
      "activeIds": [
        "humectant"
      ],
      "startedDay": 0,
      "note": "A rinse-off body and face wash, applied to the face in the shower daily. It is modelled as a humectant because the manufacturer states the product deposits \"24-hour nourishing MicroMoisture that continuously nourishes your skin all day\". That claim sets its own timescale, and the humectant window in the actives catalogue matches it: onset at day 1, assessment at day 14. Assay is therefore judging the product on the schedule its own label advertises, not on a stricter one chosen after the fact. Being rinse-off, it is a weak intervention by construction, which is stated here rather than discovered later."
    }
  ],
